 ## Remarks
 
-- **The failure is not an accident of one field.** By [[lem-lub-implies-nested-intervals]] every field with (LUB) is Archimedean, so any witness at all must be non-Archimedean; and in a non-Archimedean field the shrinking hypothesis in (NIP) is a severe restriction, because a length that tends to $0$ in the order of the field must get below every infinitesimal. That is why $K$ satisfies the shrinking form while failing the unrestricted one, and it is why $K$ can satisfy (NIP) while failing (LUB) at all.
